„­bible_version£KJV¤book'§chapter¨sections–…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFor the kingdom of heaven is like unto a man that is an householder, which went out early in the morning to hire labourers into his vineyard.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\And when he had agreed with the labourers for a penny a day, he sent them into his vineyard.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVAnd he went out about the third hour, and saw others standing idle in the marketplace,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsand said unto them; Go ye also into the vineyard, and whatsoever is right I will give you. And they went their way.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCAgain he went out about the sixth and ninth hour, and did likewise.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd about the eleventh hour he went out, and found others standing idle, and saith unto them, Why stand ye here all the day idle?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’They say unto him, Because no man hath hired us. He saith unto them, Go ye also into the vineyard; and whatsoever is right, that shall ye receive.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses™„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSo when even was come, the lord of the vineyard saith unto his steward, Call the labourers, and give them their hire, beginning from the last unto the first.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\And when they came that were hired about the eleventh hour, they received every man a penny.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
