„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNAnd when they had received it, they murmured against the goodman of the house,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…saying, These last have wrought but one hour, and thou hast made them equal unto us, which have borne the burden and heat of the day.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlBut he answered one of them, and said, Friend, I do thee no wrong: didst not thou agree with me for a penny?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRTake that thine is, and go thy way: I will give unto this last, even as unto thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^Is it not lawful for me to do what I will with mine own? Is thine eye evil, because I am good?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSSo the last shall be first, and the first last: for many be called, but few chosen.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_And Jesus going up to Jerusalem took the twelve disciples apart in the way, and said unto them,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•Behold, we go up to Jerusalem; and the Son of man shall be betrayed unto the chief priests and unto the scribes, and they shall condemn him to death,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyand shall deliver him to the Gentiles to mock, and to scourge, and to crucify him: and the third day he shall rise again.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvThen came to him the mother of Zebedee's children with her sons, worshipping him, and desiring a certain thing of him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥And he said unto her, What wilt thou? She saith unto him, Grant that these my two sons may sit, the one on thy right hand, and the other on the left, in thy kingdom.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÉBut Jesus answered and said, Ye know not what ye ask. Are ye able to drink of the cup that I shall drink of, and to be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with? They say unto him, We are able.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙøAnd he saith unto them, Ye shall drink indeed of my cup, and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with: but to sit on my right hand, and on my left, is not mine to give, but it shall be given to them for whom it is prepared of my Father.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUAnd when the ten heard it, they were moved with indignation against the two brethren.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥But Jesus called them unto him, and said, Ye know that the princes of the Gentiles exercise dominion over them, and they that are great exercise authority upon them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbBut it shall not be so among you: but whosoever will be great among you, let him be your minister;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ?and whosoever will be chief among you, let him be your servant:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoeven as the Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse"¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBAnd as they departed from Jericho, a great multitude followed him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™And, behold, two blind men sitting by the way side, when they heard that Jesus passed by, cried out, saying, Have mercy on us, O Lord, thou Son of David.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“And the multitude rebuked them, because they should hold their peace: but they cried the more, saying, Have mercy on us, O Lord, thou Son of David.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXAnd Jesus stood still, and called them, and said, What will ye that I shall do unto you?¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ5They say unto him, Lord, that our eyes may be opened.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzSo Jesus had compassion on them, and touched their eyes: and immediately their eyes received sight, and they followed him.¦layout ªlast_verse"